From bf9ca967509e7e420d42a88f5bb05e9704969975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:58:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 720/721] fix(kanban): deliver tui kanban notices at least once
 across backend replacement [daveey]

A busy chat's poller claimed (advanced last_event_id for) a card's completed
event into the in-memory _kanban_pending buffer, waiting for the turn to end.
When the serve process was replaced before the turn ended, the buffer
died with it: the board read "delivered",
the chat never got a row, and nothing retried.

- kanban_notify_subs gains inflight_from/inflight_pid/inflight_start. The tui
  poller claims durably: the claim stays in flight, owned by this process,
  until ack_notify_claim.
- The notices are written as one kanban_notice row (deduped by event key
  across the compression lineage) BEFORE the turn runs; the turn adopts that
  row as its user message; the claim is acked then. A busy transcript keeps
  the claim in flight and the batch buffered.
- recover_orphaned_notify_claims rewinds claims whose holder process is gone
  (pid + start-time fingerprint); run by the chat poller and the unloaded sweep.
  A live holder blocks other durable claimers.
- The unloaded sweep stamps kanban_event_keys so live/sweep paths dedup.

